    {
      "number": 1,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 7,
      "stem": "Points $A(1,1,1)$, $B(2,-2,5)$ and $C(3,0,3)$ define a triangle in three-dimensional space.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find $\\overrightarrow{AB}\\times\\overrightarrow{AC}$.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find the exact area of triangle ABC.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane through A, B and C.",
          "marks": 2
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A2",
              "text": "$\\overrightarrow{AB}=(1,-3,4)$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}=(2,-1,2)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\overrightarrow{AB}\\times\\overrightarrow{AC}=(-2,6,5)$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$\\text{Area}=\\frac12|\\overrightarrow{AB}\\times\\overrightarrow{AC}|$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\text{Area}=\\sqrt{65}/2$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "A normal is $(-2,6,5)$, so $-2x+6y+5z=d$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "At $A$, $d=-2+6+5=9$; hence $-2x+6y+5z=9$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$\\overrightarrow{AB}=(1,-3,4)$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}=(2,-1,2)$. $\\overrightarrow{AB}\\times\\overrightarrow{AC}=(-2,6,5)$. $\\text{Area}=\\sqrt{65}/2$. At $A$, $d=-2+6+5=9$; hence $-2x+6y+5z=9$.",
      "sourcePages": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 6,
      "stem": "Let $f(x)=x^2+ax+b+2$ and $g(x)=ax^2+bx+c-1$, where $a\\ne0$. It is given that $f(1)=g(1)$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find $c$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "The equations $f(x)=b+4$ and $g(x)=-1$ have the same two roots. Find $a$ and $b$.",
          "marks": 4
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$1+a+b+2=a+b+c-1$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$c=4$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The equations reduce to $x^2+ax-2=0$ and $ax^2+bx+c=0$; equal root sums give $-a=-b/a$, so $b=a^2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Equal root products give $-2=c/a$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "With $c=4$, $a=-2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$b=4$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$c=4$. The equations reduce to $x^2+ax-2=0$ and $ax^2+bx+c=0$; equal root sums give $-a=-b/a$, so $b=a^2$. With $c=4$, $a=-2$. $b=4$.",
      "sourcePages": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 8,
      "stem": "In this question $\\operatorname{cis}\\theta=\\cos\\theta+i\\sin\\theta$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find all three solutions of $z^3=64i$, expressing each in the form $a+bi$.",
          "marks": 6
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Hence solve $(z+2i)^3=64i$.",
          "marks": 2
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Write $z=r\\operatorname{cis}\\theta$ and $64i=64\\operatorname{cis}(\\pi/2)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$r=4$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$3\\theta=\\pi/2+2k\\pi$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\theta=\\pi/6+2k\\pi/3$, $k=0,1,2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Two roots are $2\\sqrt3+2i$ and $-2\\sqrt3+2i$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The third root is $-4i$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Subtract $2i$ from each root in part(a)."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$z=2\\sqrt3,-2\\sqrt3,-6i$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$r=4$. $\\theta=\\pi/6+2k\\pi/3$, $k=0,1,2$. Two roots are $2\\sqrt3+2i$ and $-2\\sqrt3+2i$. The third root is $-4i$. $z=2\\sqrt3,-2\\sqrt3,-6i$.",
      "sourcePages": [
        4
      ]
