    {
      "number": 5,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 6,
      "stem": "Solve $4^{x+1}\\,3^{2x+1}=18^{x+1}$, giving your answer in the form $a+\\log_2 b$, where $a$ and $b$ are integers.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "",
          "prompt": "Show your algebraic working.",
          "marks": 6
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$4^x\\cdot4\\cdot3^{2x}\\cdot3=18^x\\cdot18$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$4^x3^{2x}/18^x=18/12$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$(36/18)^x=3/2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$2^x=3/2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Take logarithms to base2."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$x=-1+\\log_2 3$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$(36/18)^x=3/2$. $2^x=3/2$. $x=-1+\\log_2 3$.",
      "sourcePages": [
        6
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 7,
      "stem": "The function $y(x)$ satisfies $\\displaystyle\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{4x^3}{1+x^4}y=5$ and $y(1)=1$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "",
          "prompt": "Find $y$ in terms of $x$.",
          "marks": 7
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "This is linear with $P(x)=4x^3/(1+x^4)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The integrating factor is $e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx}=1+x^4$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$\\frac{d}{dx}[(1+x^4)y]=5(1+x^4)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A2",
              "text": "Integrating gives $(1+x^4)y=x^5+5x+c$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$2=1+5+c$, hence $c=-4$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$y=(x^5+5x-4)/(1+x^4)$, valid for all real$x$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "The integrating factor is $e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx}=1+x^4$. Integrating gives $(1+x^4)y=x^5+5x+c$. $2=1+5+c$, hence $c=-4$. $y=(x^5+5x-4)/(1+x^4)$, valid for all real$x$.",
      "sourcePages": [
        7
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 7,
      "stem": "Let $f(x)=\\frac32x^4-\\frac13x^3-\\frac52x^2+1$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find the gradient of the tangent to the graph of $f$ at $x=-1$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find the other two values of $x$ at which the tangent is parallel to the tangent in part(a).",
          "marks": 5
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$f\\prime(x)=6x^3-x^2-5x$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$f\\prime(-1)=-2$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Solve $6x^3-x^2-5x+2=0$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "The known root$-1$ gives factor$x+1$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$6x^3-x^2-5x+2=(x+1)(6x^2-7x+2)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$x=2/3$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$x=1/2$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$f\\prime(-1)=-2$. $6x^3-x^2-5x+2=(x+1)(6x^2-7x+2)$. $x=2/3$. $x=1/2$.",
      "sourcePages": [
        8
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 7,
      "stem": "An arrangement uses each of the nine distinct digits 1 to 9 and each of three distinct symbols (dollar sign, at sign and hash sign) exactly once. Let $A$ be the number of arrangements in which the three symbols are consecutive. Let $B$ be the number in which no two symbols are consecutive.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "",
          "prompt": "By finding expressions for $A$ and $B$, show that $B=12A$.",
          "marks": 7
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "For$A$, treat the three symbols as one block alongside nine digits."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Arrange ten objects in$10!$ways."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Arrange the symbols within their block in$3!$ways: $A=10!3!$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "For$B$, the nine ordered digits make ten gaps; assign three distinct symbols to different gaps."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The gap assignment has$10\\cdot9\\cdot8$possibilities."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$B=10\\cdot9\\cdot8\\cdot9!$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$B/A=(9\\cdot8)/3!=12$, as required."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "Arrange ten objects in$10!$ways. Arrange the symbols within their block in$3!$ways: $A=10!3!$. The gap assignment has$10\\cdot9\\cdot8$possibilities. $B=10\\cdot9\\cdot8\\cdot9!$. $B/A=(9\\cdot8)/3!=12$, as required.",
      "sourcePages": [
        9
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "section": "B",
      "marks": 18,
      "stem": "In triangle $ABC$, $\\angle CAB=x^\\circ$, $\\angle ABC=2x^\\circ$ and $BC=25$. Point $D$ is the foot of the perpendicular from $C$ to $AB$. It is given that $\\sin x=3/5$ and $0<x<90$. The diagram is schematic.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find the exact values of $\\cos x$ and $\\sin 2x$.",
          "marks": 4
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find $\\cos2x$ exactly.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Find $AC$.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "d",
          "prompt": "Find $AD$.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "e",
          "prompt": "Find $BD$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "f",
          "prompt": "Hence find $AB$ and the area of triangle $ABC$.",
          "marks": 3
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Use$\\sin^2x+\\cos^2x=1$and the acute-angle condition."
            },
            {
              "code": "A2",
              "text": "$\\cos x=4/5$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\sin2x=2(3/5)(4/5)=24/25$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$\\cos2x=1-2\\sin^2x$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$1-2(3/5)^2=1-18/25$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\cos2x=7/25$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "By the sine rule,$25/\\sin x=AC/\\sin2x$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$AC=25(24/25)/(3/5)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$AC=40$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M2",
              "text": "$AD/AC=\\cos x$, with$AC=40$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$AD=32$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "e",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
